  "id": "DrugBank_DB06267 - MONDO_1780",
  "verbalization": "Udenafil, through its indication for Psychologic Dyspareunia, serves as a bridge to Tadalafil and Alprostadil, both of which are implicated in the path to Premature Ejaculation (disease). This suggests a potential mechanism where Udenafil may influence psychological factors that contribute to sexual dysfunction, which in turn could affect ejaculatory control. The indirect pathways through Tadalafil and Alprostadil highlight a possible role in modulating physiological processes related to sexual response, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a plausible but indirect link between Udenafil and Premature Ejaculation, emphasizing the need for further research to clarify the underlying biological pathways.",
